{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-22979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{95}^{∘}?$\n\n- ${625}^{∘}$\n- ${160}^{∘}$\n- $-{455}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{95}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={265}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={625}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{95}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{455}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{∘}$ and $-{455}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ec9e5856640ec362f15066f9488e2c5a8636dce9f16c6efc10999b68829746c"} {"question" "q-22979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =2\\pi $\n\n- $4\\pi $\n- $5\\pi $\n- $-2\\pi $" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\pi =4\\pi \\,✓$\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\cdot (2\\pi )=6\\pi $\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $6\\pi .$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\pi =0$\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-2\\pi \\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only $4\\pi $ and $-2\\pi $ are coterminal with $2\\pi .$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ec9e5856640ec362f15066f9488e2c5a8636dce9f16c6efc10999b68829746c"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-22984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}?$\n\n- $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$\n- $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}$\n- $-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{10\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}.$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-\\frac{14\\pi }{3}$\n\nOf the given angles, all three are coterminal with $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I, II, and III." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ec9e5856640ec362f15066f9488e2c5a8636dce9f16c6efc10999b68829746c"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II and III"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-23191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The angle $\\theta =-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ by *adding* integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is coterminal with $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/891959642b0d055d852329c59be7541179dd5ae0c4182c2bec533261ce3a700d.png)\n\nWe see that $\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ lies in quadrant IV. Therefore, $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ also lies in this quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ec9e5856640ec362f15066f9488e2c5a8636dce9f16c6efc10999b68829746c"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Between quadrants II and III"] ["text" "I"] ["text" "II"] ["text" "III"] ["text" "IV"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-34403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "IV"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The angle $\\theta =-{530}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-170$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={190}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${190}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/1e741939f538fc5dfba9b5ff6f3b4ce0e68c5ebd746dfae533d3209c0c29feba.png)\n\nWe see that ${190}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant III. Therefore, $-{530}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ec9e5856640ec362f15066f9488e2c5a8636dce9f16c6efc10999b68829746c"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Between quadrants II and III"] ["text" "I"] ["text" "II"] ["text" "III"] ["text" "IV"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"} {"question" "q-124707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/state.json" "file_sha256" "c98c70287eff13d55e9bb4916050775b6a098a5654c15d35c6d0432bddf8f19f"}] "usage" {"q-23191" [] "q-34403" []} "basis" 804 "retractions" [[17592186060141 :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $θ =-\\frac{2π}{3}$?\n\n1. $\\frac{4π}{3}$\n2. $\\frac{10π}{3}$\n3. $-\\frac{8π}{3}$"] [1759218606019